WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.269 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  four years ago  i was in a psych ward i was blindsided  by shrieks of accusations  being hurled my way you why are you  spying on me  stop following me just because i'm  famous  doesn't mean you can invade my privacy  i was a medical student at the johns  hopkins hospital when i first learned  what a delusion was a belief that is  persistently held  despite evidence to the contrary  over these past four years i've realized  just how widespread  delusions are in our society  we have grammy award-winning artists who  believe that the moon landing was faked  and we have professional basketball  players who believe that the earth is  flat  but when people put on their tinfoil  hats put tape over their webcams  and wait for the re-emergence of the  lizard people we laugh them off  instead of worrying about their mental  health but just because a conspiracy  theory is funny  doesn't mean it's a joke  deep down conspiracy theories are  symptoms of a broader problem  the fundamental attribution error or  the fae this is the tendency to prefer  explanations  based on perceived intent and motive  rather than circumstance and coincidence  today my core message to you is the fae  is alive  in your daily life i'm going to show you  three ways  in which this bias plays a role in your  life pandemic conspiracy theories  minority oppression and self-help  gospels  while flat earth truthers may seem  harmless  conspiracy theories can be more serious  than you would think  theories espoused by a q anon such as  the coven 19 virus was developed in a  lab  or the vaccine contains tracking  microchips  can have seriously damaging consequences  on the health and livelihoods  of people worldwide these theories are  often more appealing than the truth  because they offer people an illusion of  control  for many the pandemic is terrifying  poorly understood and massively  disruptive  my grandmother is one of these people  before the pandemic  she was a super social person but now  her life has been completely uprooted  and she blames it on numerous  unfounded conspiracies in a crisis like  this  it's easy for her to believe that an  evil plot  being orchestrated by evil villains all  acting in concert  is the responsible agent for the  pandemic  more challenging for her to believe is  that  the world came to a grinding halt  because one small virus  from one small bat made a series of  jumps to an unlucky man in a chinese  marketplace  because that's too insignificant  too unsatisfying a reason  for people like my grandmother they  believe these theories because of the  fae  they assign someone's ulterior motives  to the origins of the pandemic  rather than sheer chance  to change their views we must first  realize that  these people are not delusional but  rather  they too just want to understand and  have certainty  during these trying times  rather than lambasting them for their  beliefs  or censoring them on twitter we should  empathize with them  and equip them with the tools so that  they can overcome these false beliefs  on their own we need to make people more  media  and science literate research has found  that taking critical thinking classes  actually reduces your susceptibility  to conspiracy theories by making people  question the facts behind their own  beliefs as hard as that may be  they can overcome conspiracy theories  and the fae  on their own again  my core message to you today is the fae  is alive  in your life next  let's talk about minority oppression how  about a quiz  true or false hard work  talent and personal perseverance are the  keys to success  and wealth if you answered true then you  have fallen victim  to the fae in reality  the best way to die rich in america is  to be born rich  for every rags-to-riches headline we see  there are countless  untold stories of poverty and misfortune  we rush to celebrate those who succeed  against all odds  yet regularly overlook why the odds were  so long  in the first place for so many people  the levers of destiny are out of their  grasp  so why do we even overlook these odds in  the first place  society would have us believe that we  live in a just  world where the world is the way it is  for a good reason  and that those who have it bad must have  done something to deserve it  the black kid who got shot should not  have been running away from the police  the woman who was assaulted should not  have dressed that way  as someone who suffered from an eating  disorder and could not receive treatment  for over a year  i am pained when i hear people claim  that overweight and obese people should  simply  have more willpower and eat less  those in power blame individuals to  distract away  from the systemic change and empathy for  others  that our society truly needs  we must recognize this how can we hope  to change  our unequal and unfair systems in  society  if we do not recognize our own roles in  perpetuating  these beliefs  if we wish to weave equality into the  fabric of our society  we must first begin by assessing the  nature of our own convictions  the fae is alive in your daily life  next let's talk about something that i  hold dear  i love self-help books my bookshelf is  full of books  winning friends and influence and not  giving a [ __ ]  marie condos the life-changing magic of  tidying up  was as life-changing to me as the title  suggests  i even received self-help books for my  birthday  now i don't know what that says about  what my friends think about me  but i can tell you what that reveals  about what i believed  that if only i acted and behaved better  i could live  a better life our society forces this  gospel of self-help  upon all of us we're told to shore up  our inadequate abilities  fix our character flaws and overcome our  individual obstacles and weaknesses  but this approach has one crucial flaw  the fae  because it does not consider the role of  context  the problem with self-help isn't that  you're unable to help yourself  but rather it falsely promises  that you and you alone are responsible  for your successes  and failures  in reality your individual qualities  and your environment determine your  behavior  but the biggest piece of this  explanatory pie is circumstance and so  if we wish to accomplish our self-help  goals  we must structure our surroundings in  such a way  that it reduces our need to be so  self-reliant on our individual decisions  and willpower for example if you want to  eat more healthily  you shouldn't rely on your willpower to  stop you from eating all the cookies  instead you should fill your cupboards  and refrigerators with healthy snacks  instead of junk food if you want to  write that novel  you should set aside an hour every day  to jot down words instead of waiting for  inspiration to strike  if we structure our surroundings to set  us up for success  perhaps we won't have to be so hard on  ourselves in the future  so let me summarize whether through the  conspiracy theories of others  societal minority oppression or your own  beliefs about yourself  the fundamental attribution error plays  a critical role  in molding how you interact with society  and the shape of society itself  my challenge for you is to not only  become aware  of this error but also to refuse its  seductive pull  here are three ways one practice  empathy and gratitude especially when in  discussions with others about their  opinion  two practice self-awareness look inwards  and critically assess the facts that  underlie your beliefs  and three pause think about the  circumstances that could be at play  before judging others give people  the benefit of the doubt if there's one  thing you can take away from this talk  i hope it's this give yourself and  others  a break thank you  you

